#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129270 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128847 :question/id #uuid "b16845a2-5f66-524a-90ea-37f8a8186f8f" :question/math-academy-id "e-11518" :question/problem "Find the locations of all of the critical points of the transformation $\\mathbf{T},$ where $\\mathbf T$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf T: {\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{array} \\right]} \n\\longrightarrow \n{\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}w - {u}^{3} \\\\ 2 u v \\\\ {u}^{2} + v\\end{array} \\right]}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a transformation \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:{\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{array} \\right]} \\to {\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}x ( u , v , w ) \\\\ y ( u , v , w ) \\\\ z ( u , v , w )\\end{array} \\right]},\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $\\mathbf T,$ denoted $\\dfrac{\\partial (x, y, z)}{\\partial (u, v, w)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} & \\frac{∂x}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v} & \\frac{∂y}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & \\frac{∂z}{∂v} & \\frac{∂z}{∂w}\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have \n\n$$\nx(u,v,w) =w-u^3, \\qquad \ny(u,v,w) = 2uv, \\qquad\nz(u,v,w) = u^2+v.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =-3{u}^{2} & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂w} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =2v & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =2u & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂w} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & =2u & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v} & =1 & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂w} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}-3{u}^{2} & 0 & 1 \\\\ 2v & 2u & 0 \\\\ 2u & 1 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-3{u}^{2}\\begin{vmatrix}2u & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{vmatrix}+1\\begin{vmatrix}2v & 2u \\\\ 2u & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-3{u}^{2}(0-0)+1(2v-4{u}^{2}) \\\\  & =2(v-2{u}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function has critical points when $\\dfrac{\\partial (x, y, z)}{\\partial (u, v, w)} =0.$ So, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =0 \\\\ 2(v-2{u}^{2}) & =0 \\\\ v-2{u}^{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation $v-2u^2 = 0$ defines the parabolic cylinder $v=2u^2.$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b4a31c6-01be-5b15-88f5-9150f350e944" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050005 :topic/difficulty 1.177909453874124 :topic/id #uuid "25b1fb2e-aa54-5955-88cd-263118f65faa" :topic/knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124597} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124651} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124652}] :topic/math-academy-id 1898 :topic/next [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048175} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049530} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050045} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050816}] :topic/title "Identifying Quadric Surfaces"}] :knowledge-point/level-coverage [{:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186528143 :question-generator/id #uuid "df024be5-5845-52b9-a2d5-f5eab3c10414" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186129270.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129526 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "59ecd82e-c85b-5221-81f4-5aa437d23a7f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the $vw-$plane." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401290} {:answer/id #uuid "1680c5f5-1c51-52cd-a03a-ad30d3c07c77" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the parabolic cylinder $u=2{w}^{2}.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401291} {:answer/id #uuid "92c1139b-4ea6-5a6e-91ff-1cd1ee2688f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $u=2v.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401292} {:answer/id #uuid "9ea440aa-4bbc-5828-a750-3ec0ce76a35d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the parabolic cylinder $u=-{w}^{2}.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401293} {:answer/id #uuid "b1928d32-8a83-5bc0-a68f-3b8d2a17bd07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $u=w.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401294}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9ea440aa-4bbc-5828-a750-3ec0ce76a35d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the parabolic cylinder $u=-{w}^{2}.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401293} :answer-field/id #uuid "17caa721-6c88-5948-86f1-24aa0f77f9b9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401289}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "685e989d-8721-5a8c-a4d8-0e44efe4bc9b" :question/math-academy-id "q-161819" :question/problem "Find the locations of all of the critical points of the transformation $\\mathbf{T},$ where $\\mathbf{T}$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}{u}^{2}-{w}^{2} \\\\ w{e}^{u} \\\\ u-v\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a transformation \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $\\mathbf{T},$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} & \\frac{∂x}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v} & \\frac{∂y}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & \\frac{∂z}{∂v} & \\frac{∂z}{∂w}\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have \n\n$$\nx(u,v,w)={u}^{2}-{w}^{2},\\,y(u,v,w)=w{e}^{u},\\,z(u,v,w)=u-v.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =2u & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂w} & =-2w \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =w{e}^{u} & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂w} & ={e}^{u} \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & =1 & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v} & =-1 & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂w} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}2u & 0 & -2w \\\\ w{e}^{u} & 0 & {e}^{u} \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2u\\begin{vmatrix}0 & {e}^{u} \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{vmatrix}-2w\\begin{vmatrix}w{e}^{u} & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2u(0+{e}^{u})-2w(-w{e}^{u}-0) \\\\  & =2u{e}^{u}+2{w}^{2}{e}^{u} \\\\  & =2{e}^{u}({w}^{2}+u).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function has critical points when $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}=0.$ So, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =0 \\\\ 2{e}^{u}({w}^{2}+u) & =0 \\\\ {w}^{2}+u & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation ${w}^{2}+u=0$ defines the parabolic cylinder $u=-{w}^{2}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129754 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "89f2fafa-94fa-537a-9de2-cde9b153270f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the $vw-$plane." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402683} {:answer/id #uuid "06b7dea6-5d67-5db6-9562-564a467e6927" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the sphere ${u}^{2}+{v}^{2}+{w}^{2}=1.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402684} {:answer/id #uuid "5cdabe0b-331f-59b0-be6a-e0b333cf7d10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the parabolic cylinder ${w}^{2}=2u.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402685} {:answer/id #uuid "edca51bc-5f25-52b9-81ee-5e945aaea583" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $w=u.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402686} {:answer/id #uuid "2daa5374-5e80-5f12-9e7f-d5612c496bb5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the $uv-$plane." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402687}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "89f2fafa-94fa-537a-9de2-cde9b153270f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the $vw-$plane." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402683} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec45c948-28d5-5ad6-a116-f2bf6a3a31b0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402682}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ab44c8de-700d-51cc-ab4a-3755f7926aef" :question/math-academy-id "q-39709" :question/problem "Find the locations of all of the critical points of the transformation $\\mathbf{T},$ where $\\mathbf{T}$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}{u}^{2}-v \\\\ {u}^{2}+v \\\\ {e}^{w}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a transformation \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $\\mathbf{T},$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} & \\frac{∂x}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v} & \\frac{∂y}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & \\frac{∂z}{∂v} & \\frac{∂z}{∂w}\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have \n\n$$\nx(u,v,w)={u}^{2}-v,\\,y(u,v,w)={u}^{2}+v,\\,z(u,v,w)={e}^{w}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =2u & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =-1 & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂w} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =2u & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =1 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂w} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂w} & ={e}^{w}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}2u & -1 & 0 \\\\ 2u & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & {e}^{w}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & ={e}^{w}\\begin{vmatrix}2u & -1 \\\\ 2u & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & ={e}^{w}(2u+2u) \\\\  & =4u{e}^{w}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function has critical points when $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}=0.$ So, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =0 \\\\ 4u{e}^{w} & =0 \\\\ u & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation $u=0$ defines the plane $u=0,$ i.e., $vw$-plane."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281338 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b1e167f-c36b-51bb-8f7d-1c5abfba9d3c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the cylinder ${v}^{2}+{u}^{2}=1.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278842} {:answer/id #uuid "398d98c4-80d9-5695-9ad1-7904a7156b87" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the $uv-$plane." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279097} {:answer/id #uuid "50abbce6-3f16-512e-a087-34dc285e7cbe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $v=u.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279329} {:answer/id #uuid "cc12c5cd-4583-53a4-9f13-8cababa0d611" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the parabolic cylinder $v={u}^{2}.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280382} {:answer/id #uuid "de43abc5-071a-5046-a899-84beee7c637b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the $uw-$plane." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280551}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "50abbce6-3f16-512e-a087-34dc285e7cbe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $v=u.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279329} :answer-field/id #uuid "73950424-d736-5015-94bb-837d8bf513c9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281040}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d47d2404-bd86-5706-ba43-4f015172617a" :question/math-academy-id "q-161809" :question/problem "Find the locations of all of the critical points of the transformation $\\mathbf{T},$ where $\\mathbf{T}$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}uv \\\\ u+v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a transformation \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $\\mathbf{T},$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} & \\frac{∂x}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v} & \\frac{∂y}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & \\frac{∂z}{∂v} & \\frac{∂z}{∂w}\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have \n\n$$\nx(u,v,w)=uv,\\,y(u,v,w)=u+v,\\,z(u,v,w)=w.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =v & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =u & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂w} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =1 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =1 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂w} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂w} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}v & u & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\begin{vmatrix}v & u \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =v-u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function has critical points when $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}=0.$ So, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =0 \\\\ v-u & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation $v-u=0$ defines the plane $v=u..$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281339 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "710d7d7d-97b4-592f-b30c-acf388d38859" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the parabolic cylinder $v={w}^{2}.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279617} {:answer/id #uuid "76ca4acf-773c-501c-ba6e-25239ada0435" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the $vw-$plane." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279651} {:answer/id #uuid "7b363e77-7f40-535f-a3a7-6bd580690682" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $v=2w.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279692} {:answer/id #uuid "88ce4141-06f6-5738-b4cf-0fb6b9a3a05e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the planes $v=\\pm w.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279813} {:answer/id #uuid "eaed37b4-3321-5a47-9faa-28666138fd1b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $v=u.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280655}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "88ce4141-06f6-5738-b4cf-0fb6b9a3a05e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the planes $v=\\pm w.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279813} :answer-field/id #uuid "bcf9576c-0ce8-5723-bb46-cfba69aeb672" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281170}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f26bca76-37a5-5f68-8e4a-4d9215b02535" :question/math-academy-id "q-161812" :question/problem "Find the locations of all of the critical points of the transformation $\\mathbf{T},$ where $\\mathbf{T}$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ {v}^{3}+{w}^{3} \\\\ v+w\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a transformation \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $\\mathbf{T},$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} & \\frac{∂x}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v} & \\frac{∂y}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & \\frac{∂z}{∂v} & \\frac{∂z}{∂w}\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have \n\n$$\nx(u,v,w)=u,\\,y(u,v,w)={v}^{3}+{w}^{3},\\,z(u,v,w)=v+w.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =1 & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂w} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =3{v}^{2} & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂w} & =3{w}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v} & =1 & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂w} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3{v}^{2} & 3{w}^{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\begin{vmatrix}3{v}^{2} & 3{w}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1(3{v}^{2}-3{w}^{2}) \\\\  & =3({v}^{2}-{w}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function has critical points when $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}=0.$ So, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =0 \\\\ 3({v}^{2}-{w}^{2}) & =0 \\\\ {v}^{2}-{w}^{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation ${v}^{2}-{w}^{2}=0$ defines a pair of intersecting planes $v=w$ and $v=-w.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281340 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e5c045a-d984-5c99-8fa3-0129ac115c4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the parabolic cylinder $v={w}^{2}.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278721} {:answer/id #uuid "2d089752-d1ca-57d4-aaad-39bd60fd867f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the $vw-$plane." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278988} {:answer/id #uuid "768c6810-e6a9-5693-b6ba-88bee24c33f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the $uv-$plane." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279649} {:answer/id #uuid "9f89b797-8be9-5dae-9e56-f0b7e9d1b9f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the sphere ${u}^{2}+{v}^{2}+{w}^{2}=2.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280008} {:answer/id #uuid "bc5b203f-69ef-5d8b-b9f1-3986949f0305" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $u=w.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280247}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "768c6810-e6a9-5693-b6ba-88bee24c33f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the $uv-$plane." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279649} :answer-field/id #uuid "55be6ad3-d866-57e2-8467-8385c57eb9ce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280977}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e2d2dfd0-abce-5610-a53e-633420f43575" :question/math-academy-id "q-161815" :question/problem "Find the locations of all of the critical points of the transformation $\\mathbf{T},$ where $\\mathbf{T}$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{u} \\\\ vw \\\\ u+w\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a transformation \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $\\mathbf{T},$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} & \\frac{∂x}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v} & \\frac{∂y}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & \\frac{∂z}{∂v} & \\frac{∂z}{∂w}\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have \n\n$$\nx(u,v,w)=\\sqrt{u},\\,y(u,v,w)=vw,\\,z(u,v,w)=u+w.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}} & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂w} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =w & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂w} & =v \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & =1 & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂w} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & w & v \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}}\\begin{vmatrix}w & v \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}+1\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ w & v\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}}(w-0)+0 \\\\  & =\\frac{w}{2\\sqrt{u}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function has critical points when $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}=0.$ So, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{w}{2\\sqrt{u}} & =0 \\\\ w & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation $w=0$ defines the plane $w=0,$ i.e., $uv$-plane."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281341 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "012e5e71-30c4-576f-9027-84673f0cec11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the sphere ${u}^{2}+{v}^{2}+{w}^{2}=3.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278593} {:answer/id #uuid "1ca3f8ee-ee06-5aa0-b1ee-b1a91215f89a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $v=3.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278855} {:answer/id #uuid "aedf9c47-b56b-5e71-845a-05c0a9e74384" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the cylinder ${v}^{2}+{w}^{2}=0.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280139} {:answer/id #uuid "f4e3d435-b0b0-5133-a7de-47ee24110c94" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the $uw-$plane." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280736} {:answer/id #uuid "f7242b75-d7a6-5b47-a2a4-a6f542bd4ba3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the $uv-$plane." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280754}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1ca3f8ee-ee06-5aa0-b1ee-b1a91215f89a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $v=3.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278855} :answer-field/id #uuid "b0414cad-2a72-50dc-8e82-0bf67299254f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281140}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5ae1d4bd-a84e-5282-96ec-f8259badfc91" :question/math-academy-id "q-161817" :question/problem "Find the locations of all of the critical points of the transformation $\\mathbf{T},$ where $\\mathbf{T}$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v{e}^{w} \\\\ 2u+v+3w\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a transformation \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $\\mathbf{T},$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} & \\frac{∂x}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v} & \\frac{∂y}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & \\frac{∂z}{∂v} & \\frac{∂z}{∂w}\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have \n\n$$\nx(u,v,w)=u,\\,y(u,v,w)=v{e}^{w},\\,z(u,v,w)=2u+v+3w.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =1 & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂w} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & ={e}^{w} & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂w} & =v{e}^{w} \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & =2 & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v} & =1 & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂w} & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & {e}^{w} & v{e}^{w} \\\\ 2 & 1 & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\begin{vmatrix}{e}^{w} & v{e}^{w} \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1(3{e}^{w}-v{e}^{w}) \\\\  & ={e}^{w}(3-v).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function has critical points when $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}=0.$ So, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{w}(3-v) & =0 \\\\ 3-v & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation $3-v=0$ defines the plane $v=3.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281342 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0360b3bf-0e11-5644-974a-fb91e4539e1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the parabolic cylinder $w=\\frac{{v}^{2}}{2}.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278610} {:answer/id #uuid "40d23535-8e40-5b39-96da-dc0c5913b017" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the planes $v=\\pm w.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279167} {:answer/id #uuid "4d4e4c43-7095-567c-8087-ac111d00d4b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $v=u.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279286} {:answer/id #uuid "a24f7a5b-f9c2-51ab-bfe8-2b6ef54faa12" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the $uw-$ plane." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280034} {:answer/id #uuid "c0ca341c-0372-5300-8b3a-24814e46f956" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $v=\\frac{3}{4}.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280285}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c0ca341c-0372-5300-8b3a-24814e46f956" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $v=\\frac{3}{4}.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280285} :answer-field/id #uuid "0966bd13-e522-5f74-88dd-66c421ecae33" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280850}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5828c68b-3870-5e91-8f73-8351ac68b7ad" :question/math-academy-id "q-161818" :question/problem "Find the locations of all of the critical points of the transformation $\\mathbf{T},$ where $\\mathbf{T}$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}u+3w \\\\ v+2w \\\\ {v}^{2}-u\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a transformation \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $\\mathbf{T},$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} & \\frac{∂x}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v} & \\frac{∂y}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & \\frac{∂z}{∂v} & \\frac{∂z}{∂w}\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have \n\n$$\nx(u,v,w)=u+3w,\\,y(u,v,w)=v+2w,\\,z(u,v,w)={v}^{2}-u.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =1 & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂w} & =3 \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =1 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂w} & =2 \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & =-1 & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v} & =2v & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂w} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2v & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 2v & 0\\end{vmatrix}+3\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2v\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1(0-4v)+3(0+1) \\\\  & =3-4v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function has critical points when $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}=0.$ So, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =0 \\\\ 3-4v & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation $3-4v=0$ defines the plane $v=\\frac{3}{4}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186376124 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07b9f18b-ec2f-51d5-ae14-92461f9907ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the $wv-$plane." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376126} {:answer/id #uuid "5bacd98b-62c2-5e98-a210-80793aec69cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $w=v.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376127} {:answer/id #uuid "13bfe028-f756-50dc-a99d-e4bd7e879772" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the parabolic cylinder $w=2{v}^{2}.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376128} {:answer/id #uuid "8ad07193-94a4-5bd2-b02f-54c7365c5656" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $w=-2v.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376129} {:answer/id #uuid "69b5ad50-abba-5674-a016-be9139fe02be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the $uv-$plane." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376130}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "13bfe028-f756-50dc-a99d-e4bd7e879772" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the parabolic cylinder $w=2{v}^{2}.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376128} :answer-field/id #uuid "88cb516a-a7eb-5761-97af-05385415c8d5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376125}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a710b40d-30b7-5142-a877-a2aee690f184" :question/math-academy-id "q-161813" :question/problem "Find the locations of all of the critical points of the transformation $\\mathbf{T},$ where $\\mathbf{T}$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{u} \\\\ {v}^{2}+w \\\\ vw\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a transformation \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $\\mathbf{T},$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} & \\frac{∂x}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v} & \\frac{∂y}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & \\frac{∂z}{∂v} & \\frac{∂z}{∂w}\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have \n\n$$\nx(u,v,w)=\\frac{1}{u},\\,y(u,v,w)={v}^{2}+w,\\,z(u,v,w)=vw.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =-\\frac{1}{{u}^{2}} & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂w} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =2v & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂w} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v} & =w & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂w} & =v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}-\\frac{1}{{u}^{2}} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2v & 1 \\\\ 0 & w & v\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{u}^{2}}\\begin{vmatrix}2v & 1 \\\\ w & v\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{u}^{2}}(2{v}^{2}-w).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function has critical points when $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}=0.$ So, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =0 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{{u}^{2}}(2{v}^{2}-w) & =0 \\\\ w-2{v}^{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation $w-2{v}^{2}=0$ defines the parabolic cylinder $w=2{v}^{2}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186401275 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "53f14d31-90ea-5326-97dc-45022d0835ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $u+v-2w=0.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401277} {:answer/id #uuid "b740b568-485c-5311-a423-33ea2f3eeffb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the elliptic cylinder ${u}^{2}+2{w}^{2}=1.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401278} {:answer/id #uuid "a6795027-5482-5bff-8214-2dd2cc097fe2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the parabolic cylinder $v={u}^{2}.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401279} {:answer/id #uuid "5adbc1f1-362c-537c-bb50-2cdecc09b123" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the $vw-$ plane." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401280} {:answer/id #uuid "f3a89ced-7070-57be-88cf-4d4b894bd3f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $u=2w.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401281}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f3a89ced-7070-57be-88cf-4d4b894bd3f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $u=2w.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401281} :answer-field/id #uuid "65676948-b2fa-585d-8619-ca89f50c6f34" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401276}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d8752c18-2285-5bd2-a3b2-ba4d0420bd04" :question/math-academy-id "q-161814" :question/problem "Find the locations of all of the critical points of the transformation $\\mathbf{T},$ where $\\mathbf{T}$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}u+2w \\\\ v-u \\\\ uw\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a transformation \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $\\mathbf{T},$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} & \\frac{∂x}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v} & \\frac{∂y}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & \\frac{∂z}{∂v} & \\frac{∂z}{∂w}\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have \n\n$$\nx(u,v,w)=u+2w,\\,y(u,v,w)=v-u,\\,z(u,v,w)=uw.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =1 & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂w} & =2 \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =-1 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =1 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂w} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & =w & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂w} & =u\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ w & 0 & u\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & u\\end{vmatrix}+2\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ w & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1(u-0)+2(0-w) \\\\  & =u-2w.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function has critical points when $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}=0.$ So, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =0 \\\\ u-2w & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation $u-2w=0$ defines the plane $u=2w.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186401282 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b76c85a4-c631-5c36-941d-c14613479d8a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the $vw-$plane." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401284} {:answer/id #uuid "10a3627e-14c0-553d-8005-b8e65337d0b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the parabolic cylinder $w=-2{v}^{2}.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401285} {:answer/id #uuid "b1ffd8d2-f852-57f7-9970-8454309f0281" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $2u+v+w=0.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401286} {:answer/id #uuid "a8fe9b5d-4fbe-56d7-9627-c5c1df64a715" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $w=-2u.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401287} {:answer/id #uuid "e3cbb05e-806b-56aa-8136-04b088a6dc5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the parabolic cylinder $w={u}^{2}.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401288}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b76c85a4-c631-5c36-941d-c14613479d8a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the $vw-$plane." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401284} :answer-field/id #uuid "175d9200-8100-5e54-b984-b7451df1967c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401283}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fc380b3f-d92e-5c45-8651-fac240787b92" :question/math-academy-id "q-161816" :question/problem "Find the locations of all of the critical points of the transformation $\\mathbf{T},$ where $\\mathbf{T}$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{u} \\\\ {e}^{u+w} \\\\ uv+w\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a transformation \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $\\mathbf{T},$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} & \\frac{∂x}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v} & \\frac{∂y}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & \\frac{∂z}{∂v} & \\frac{∂z}{∂w}\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have \n\n$$\nx(u,v,w)={e}^{u},\\,y(u,v,w)={e}^{u+w},\\,z(u,v,w)=uv+w.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & ={e}^{u} & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂w} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & ={e}^{u+w} & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂w} & ={e}^{u+w} \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & =v & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v} & =u & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂w} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}{e}^{u} & 0 & 0 \\\\ {e}^{u+w} & 0 & {e}^{u+w} \\\\ v & u & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & ={e}^{u}\\begin{vmatrix}0 & {e}^{u+w} \\\\ u & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & ={e}^{u}(0-u{e}^{u+w}) \\\\  & =-u{e}^{2u+w}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function has critical points when $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}=0.$ So, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =0 \\\\ -u{e}^{2u+w} & =0 \\\\ u & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation $u=0$ defines the plane $u=0,$ i.e., $vw$-plane."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406771 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06cfa4e4-4978-5d07-b498-b67163d323ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the $uw-$plane." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406760} {:answer/id #uuid "47f0e73b-3fcc-5922-ac4c-5cbbb15dc078" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the sphere ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=1.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406762} {:answer/id #uuid "4cd27081-6df8-5fcc-87e8-0b763e12dd24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the $vw-$plane." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406763} {:answer/id #uuid "bdd4d236-b060-5654-b754-6a3374d3448b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $v=1.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406766} {:answer/id #uuid "ddaabaf5-f0e8-54a9-9f5a-d6c4751feaf2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $v=u.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406768}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "06cfa4e4-4978-5d07-b498-b67163d323ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the $uw-$plane." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406760} :answer-field/id #uuid "06a97003-66fd-5b44-944b-7b4ac3d8364b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406769}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "84951e54-c705-5b01-85eb-275b777e397c" :question/math-academy-id "q-161810" :question/problem "Find the locations of all of the critical points of the transformation $\\mathbf{T},$ where $\\mathbf{T}$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}u+vw \\\\ {v}^{2} \\\\ w+v\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a transformation \n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} & \\frac{∂x}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v} & \\frac{∂y}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & \\frac{∂z}{∂v} & \\frac{∂z}{∂w}\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have \n\n$$\nx(u,v,w)=u+vw,\\,y(u,v,w)={v}^{2},\\,z(u,v,w)=w+v.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =1 & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =w & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂w} & =v \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =2v & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂w} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v} & =1 & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂w} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & w & v \\\\ 0 & 2v & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\begin{vmatrix}2v & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1(2v-0) \\\\  & =2v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function has critical points when $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}=0.$ So, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =0 \\\\ 2v & =0 \\\\ v & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation $v=0$ defines the plane $v=0,$ i.e., $uw$-plane."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424180 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e37282e-8869-5ad2-9f01-e062a7d21846" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the parabolic cylinder $v=2{w}^{2}.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424153} {:answer/id #uuid "4a31e95b-7336-5699-a485-0b22a7563452" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $v=w.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424154} {:answer/id #uuid "56201c08-96c0-58d8-9ed7-c9a2a6ecea11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the $vw-$plane." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424156} {:answer/id #uuid "7447254c-742a-5c7f-adb1-193a3168832a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the $uv-$plane." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424159} {:answer/id #uuid "7473d403-04c8-5521-92cd-20ba6d10f904" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the sphere ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=4.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424160}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4a31e95b-7336-5699-a485-0b22a7563452" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $v=w.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424154} :answer-field/id #uuid "d0a37030-5cd9-5e43-a291-e19dfc94c67f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424176}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b50230b8-d517-560a-9ede-747bedde3c3c" :question/math-academy-id "q-161811" :question/problem "Find the locations of all of the critical points of the transformation $\\mathbf{T},$ where $\\mathbf{T}$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{u}+v \\\\ v+w \\\\ vw\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a transformation \n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} & \\frac{∂x}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v} & \\frac{∂y}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & \\frac{∂z}{∂v} & \\frac{∂z}{∂w}\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have \n\n$$\nx(u,v,w)={e}^{u}+v,\\,y(u,v,w)=v+w,\\,z(u,v,w)=vw.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & ={e}^{u} & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =1 & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂w} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =1 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂w} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v} & =w & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂w} & =v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}{e}^{u} & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & w & v\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & ={e}^{u}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ w & v\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & ={e}^{u}(v-w).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function has critical points when $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}=0.$ So, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{u}(v-w) & =0 \\\\ v-w & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation $v-w=0$ defines the plane $v=w.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186528079 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c605152-901c-5bcd-a252-1ab9cc3b85cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $v - 5=0.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528089} {:answer/id #uuid "4ccdd355-67c6-5566-941a-b4d92d487572" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $w - 5=0.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528091} {:answer/id #uuid "7a6eefd5-a305-5c5a-a520-b6206a7fba35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $u + 5=0.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528103} {:answer/id #uuid "849ed888-6be5-543b-abea-d73096054d02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $u - 5=0.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528107} {:answer/id #uuid "de8bd9d8-b442-57a1-9562-0a7b92d7a125" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $u=0.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528130}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "849ed888-6be5-543b-abea-d73096054d02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $u - 5=0.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528107} :answer-field/id #uuid "b12d9169-ece2-5f8e-8851-d1d9eb933e79" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528118}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "13f0dd3d-1f22-5629-9241-573d35d65b91" :question/problem "Find the locations of all of the critical points of the transformation $T,$ where $T$ is defined as\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}\\left(u - 5\\right)^{2} \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a transformation \n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} & \\frac{∂x}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v} & \\frac{∂y}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & \\frac{∂z}{∂v} & \\frac{∂z}{∂w}\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have \n\n$$\nx(u,v,w)=\\left(u - 5\\right)^{2},\\,y(u,v,w)=v,\\,z(u,v,w)=w.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =2 u - 10 & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =0 & \\frac{∂x}{∂w} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =0 & \\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =1 & \\frac{∂y}{∂w} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & =0 & \\frac{∂z}{∂v} & =0 & \\frac{∂z}{∂w} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}2 u - 10 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(2 u - 10)\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(2 u - 10)(1\\cdot(1)-(0)\\cdot(0)) \\\\  & =2 \\left(u - 5\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function has critical points when $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}=0.$ So, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =0 \\\\ 2 \\left(u - 5\\right) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe critical points lie on the plane $u - 5=0.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186528093 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25c5ea31-efda-54a4-824d-91f820e8d0c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $v=0.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528083} {:answer/id #uuid "838578b3-3790-5776-a4b4-78337049deeb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $w + 3=0.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528106} {:answer/id #uuid "950067b2-bb47-5fdd-8170-76f27c144f53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $v + 3=0.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528111} {:answer/id #uuid "e5804f4d-5f9e-5bb8-8479-505629b0e11c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $v - 3=0.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528133} {:answer/id #uuid "e72cbe6b-50cf-5c52-be21-06b2588b4072" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $u + 3=0.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528134}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "950067b2-bb47-5fdd-8170-76f27c144f53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $v + 3=0.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528111} :answer-field/id #uuid "092be8c7-b2b3-55de-a763-e9f8866ddd74" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528074}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "508d0b30-7080-5a0a-bcfa-a8afc4979721" :question/problem "Find the locations of all of the critical points of the transformation $T,$ where $T$ is defined as\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ \\left(v + 3\\right)^{2} \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a transformation \n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} & \\frac{∂x}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v} & \\frac{∂y}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & \\frac{∂z}{∂v} & \\frac{∂z}{∂w}\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have \n\n$$\nx(u,v,w)=u,\\,y(u,v,w)=\\left(v + 3\\right)^{2},\\,z(u,v,w)=w.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =1 & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =0 & \\frac{∂x}{∂w} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =0 & \\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =2 v + 6 & \\frac{∂y}{∂w} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & =0 & \\frac{∂z}{∂v} & =0 & \\frac{∂z}{∂w} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 v + 6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(1)\\begin{vmatrix}2 v + 6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(1)(2 v + 6\\cdot(1)-(0)\\cdot(0)) \\\\  & =2 \\left(v + 3\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function has critical points when $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}=0.$ So, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =0 \\\\ 2 \\left(v + 3\\right) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe critical points lie on the plane $v + 3=0.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186528094 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0544780e-14fc-55aa-87a9-4cf97780c7b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $u - 4=0.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528073} {:answer/id #uuid "0ac687cb-668d-5381-8fcb-bc9f45907122" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $u=0.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528076} {:answer/id #uuid "243e7eac-20cf-57d0-9916-6cd6a9affdcf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $u + 4=0.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528082} {:answer/id #uuid "6188d987-5745-5f88-ab24-c44d274474c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $v + 4=0.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528097} {:answer/id #uuid "be7ae697-cd3e-5479-8ce6-7405cb76bcf6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $w + 4=0.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528123}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "243e7eac-20cf-57d0-9916-6cd6a9affdcf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $u + 4=0.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528082} :answer-field/id #uuid "73995b19-08e6-5555-850a-91dc308e452a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528101}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5623f019-5b29-5f61-95d8-7be3055bcc58" :question/problem "Find the locations of all of the critical points of the transformation $T,$ where $T$ is defined as\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}\\left(u + 4\\right)^{2} \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a transformation \n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} & \\frac{∂x}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v} & \\frac{∂y}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & \\frac{∂z}{∂v} & \\frac{∂z}{∂w}\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have \n\n$$\nx(u,v,w)=\\left(u + 4\\right)^{2},\\,y(u,v,w)=v,\\,z(u,v,w)=w.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =2 u + 8 & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =0 & \\frac{∂x}{∂w} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =0 & \\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =1 & \\frac{∂y}{∂w} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & =0 & \\frac{∂z}{∂v} & =0 & \\frac{∂z}{∂w} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}2 u + 8 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(2 u + 8)\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(2 u + 8)(1\\cdot(1)-(0)\\cdot(0)) \\\\  & =2 \\left(u + 4\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function has critical points when $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}=0.$ So, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =0 \\\\ 2 \\left(u + 4\\right) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe critical points lie on the plane $u + 4=0.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186528105 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e0e693a-bf37-56cc-8164-00f372dad8fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $w - 3=0.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528085} {:answer/id #uuid "47c6ada3-a010-56e0-b46b-ae779b5a5a22" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $v - 3=0.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528087} {:answer/id #uuid "b88e5b00-228f-52e3-8b9f-d0daf74eff3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $w + 3=0.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528121} {:answer/id #uuid "c0886689-a8e4-56c9-b290-4b350e321665" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $u - 3=0.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528124} {:answer/id #uuid "c380da40-2559-5607-aa89-97268521c7a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $w=0.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528125}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2e0e693a-bf37-56cc-8164-00f372dad8fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $w - 3=0.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528085} :answer-field/id #uuid "a216c380-f1cd-5afe-ae7d-6797caccf711" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528113}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "828da370-4d6a-5438-a9e4-3248998e835e" :question/problem "Find the locations of all of the critical points of the transformation $T,$ where $T$ is defined as\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ \\left(w - 3\\right)^{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a transformation \n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} & \\frac{∂x}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v} & \\frac{∂y}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & \\frac{∂z}{∂v} & \\frac{∂z}{∂w}\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have \n\n$$\nx(u,v,w)=u,\\,y(u,v,w)=v,\\,z(u,v,w)=\\left(w - 3\\right)^{2}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =1 & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =0 & \\frac{∂x}{∂w} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =0 & \\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =1 & \\frac{∂y}{∂w} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & =0 & \\frac{∂z}{∂v} & =0 & \\frac{∂z}{∂w} & =2 w - 6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 w - 6\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(1)\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 w - 6\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(1)(1\\cdot(2 w - 6)-(0)\\cdot(0)) \\\\  & =2 \\left(w - 3\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function has critical points when $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}=0.$ So, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =0 \\\\ 2 \\left(w - 3\\right) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe critical points lie on the plane $w - 3=0.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186528109 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09e0ebbd-8383-5c1b-a7c9-4716ac9c4cc2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $16 u + 5=0.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528075} {:answer/id #uuid "0ae41af4-df52-5568-92f7-9afd52f5550d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $10 u + 4=0.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528077} {:answer/id #uuid "29353d26-c816-529b-a53d-9616a3cd2090" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $10 u + 5=0.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528084} {:answer/id #uuid "ae558e9c-6c07-5dc0-80dd-f187e7aa012e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $22 u + 5=0.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528117} {:answer/id #uuid "b236eac3-d86c-5cb2-8a40-76e176e96493" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $1 - 6 u=0.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528119}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "29353d26-c816-529b-a53d-9616a3cd2090" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $10 u + 5=0.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528084} :answer-field/id #uuid "f5b9202d-16e9-5fe8-8a86-ac05c266ac48" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528137}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9192e177-97db-5aba-a9ef-4ed8595bf5b0" :question/problem "Find the locations of all of the critical points of the transformation $T,$ where $T$ is defined as\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}u - 3 v - 2 w \\\\ - u^{2} + v \\\\ 4 u^{2} + 2 u + w\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a transformation \n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} & \\frac{∂x}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v} & \\frac{∂y}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & \\frac{∂z}{∂v} & \\frac{∂z}{∂w}\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have \n\n$$\nx(u,v,w)=u - 3 v - 2 w,\\,y(u,v,w)=- u^{2} + v,\\,z(u,v,w)=4 u^{2} + 2 u + w.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =1 & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =-3 & \\frac{∂x}{∂w} & =-2 \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =- 2 u & \\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =1 & \\frac{∂y}{∂w} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & =8 u + 2 & \\frac{∂z}{∂v} & =0 & \\frac{∂z}{∂w} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ - 2 u & 1 & 0 \\\\ 8 u + 2 & 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(1)\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}+(3)\\begin{vmatrix}- 2 u & 0 \\\\ 8 u + 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix}+(-2)\\begin{vmatrix}- 2 u & 1 \\\\ 8 u + 2 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(1)(1\\cdot(1)-(0)\\cdot(0))+(3)(- 2 u\\cdot(1)-(0)\\cdot(8 u + 2))+(-2)(- 2 u\\cdot(0)-(1)\\cdot(8 u + 2)) \\\\  & =5 \\left(2 u + 1\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function has critical points when $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}=0.$ So, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =0 \\\\ 5 \\left(2 u + 1\\right) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe critical points lie on the plane $10 u + 5=0.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186528110 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1fb84bc4-7b45-548e-a2fa-9858922eca5d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $6 u - 2=0.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528081} {:answer/id #uuid "4d84d0f3-3275-5916-8633-e0db4b4fb7b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $6 u - 3=0.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528092} {:answer/id #uuid "72856a29-c86d-552c-a63a-1b5dc73976b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $- 10 u - 2=0.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528100} {:answer/id #uuid "a617f30b-32a8-54ec-b573-dc1cd8d1f259" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $8 u + 1=0.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528115} {:answer/id #uuid "f842f30b-6f61-5ed3-882a-e4618de3d746" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $- 2 u - 2=0.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528138}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1fb84bc4-7b45-548e-a2fa-9858922eca5d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $6 u - 2=0.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528081} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a1bef16-c94d-59b0-9fff-4586e97270e2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528099}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "93ef6ca3-680b-56f1-b387-2cba8288a0cb" :question/problem "Find the locations of all of the critical points of the transformation $T,$ where $T$ is defined as\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}u + 4 v - w \\\\ - u^{2} + v \\\\ - u^{2} - 3 u + w\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a transformation \n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} & \\frac{∂x}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v} & \\frac{∂y}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & \\frac{∂z}{∂v} & \\frac{∂z}{∂w}\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have \n\n$$\nx(u,v,w)=u + 4 v - w,\\,y(u,v,w)=- u^{2} + v,\\,z(u,v,w)=- u^{2} - 3 u + w.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =1 & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =4 & \\frac{∂x}{∂w} & =-1 \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =- 2 u & \\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =1 & \\frac{∂y}{∂w} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & =- 2 u - 3 & \\frac{∂z}{∂v} & =0 & \\frac{∂z}{∂w} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 4 & -1 \\\\ - 2 u & 1 & 0 \\\\ - 2 u - 3 & 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(1)\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}+(-4)\\begin{vmatrix}- 2 u & 0 \\\\ - 2 u - 3 & 1\\end{vmatrix}+(-1)\\begin{vmatrix}- 2 u & 1 \\\\ - 2 u - 3 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(1)(1\\cdot(1)-(0)\\cdot(0))+(-4)(- 2 u\\cdot(1)-(0)\\cdot(- 2 u - 3))+(-1)(- 2 u\\cdot(0)-(1)\\cdot(- 2 u - 3)) \\\\  & =2 \\left(3 u - 1\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function has critical points when $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}=0.$ So, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =0 \\\\ 2 \\left(3 u - 1\\right) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe critical points lie on the plane $6 u - 2=0.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186528126 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c8103d5-1d1d-5539-8a25-78db0f5145f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $- 28 u - 2=0.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528078} {:answer/id #uuid "5fb0e10d-b288-5c1d-aac9-e69ffceddfec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $4 u - 1=0.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528096} {:answer/id #uuid "a9e85cfe-b159-56b8-b8f5-f5869b13e490" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $- 28 u - 1=0.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528116} {:answer/id #uuid "b3a3c49c-fbe3-52d1-a80e-087d00635c13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $36 u - 1=0.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528120} {:answer/id #uuid "f9524462-e914-593a-bd38-f2a07ae601da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $1 - 32 u=0.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528140}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a9e85cfe-b159-56b8-b8f5-f5869b13e490" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $- 28 u - 1=0.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528116} :answer-field/id #uuid "47e0a85e-166a-5bfd-8b30-c8fcd72abd92" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528088}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "cb745fb6-ba80-5128-902d-8b91b00fe021" :question/problem "Find the locations of all of the critical points of the transformation $T,$ where $T$ is defined as\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}u - 4 v - 2 w \\\\ - 4 u^{2} + v \\\\ u^{2} - u + w\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a transformation \n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} & \\frac{∂x}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v} & \\frac{∂y}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & \\frac{∂z}{∂v} & \\frac{∂z}{∂w}\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have \n\n$$\nx(u,v,w)=u - 4 v - 2 w,\\,y(u,v,w)=- 4 u^{2} + v,\\,z(u,v,w)=u^{2} - u + w.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =1 & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =-4 & \\frac{∂x}{∂w} & =-2 \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =- 8 u & \\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =1 & \\frac{∂y}{∂w} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & =2 u - 1 & \\frac{∂z}{∂v} & =0 & \\frac{∂z}{∂w} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -4 & -2 \\\\ - 8 u & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 u - 1 & 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(1)\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}+(4)\\begin{vmatrix}- 8 u & 0 \\\\ 2 u - 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix}+(-2)\\begin{vmatrix}- 8 u & 1 \\\\ 2 u - 1 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(1)(1\\cdot(1)-(0)\\cdot(0))+(4)(- 8 u\\cdot(1)-(0)\\cdot(2 u - 1))+(-2)(- 8 u\\cdot(0)-(1)\\cdot(2 u - 1)) \\\\  & =- 28 u - 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function has critical points when $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}=0.$ So, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =0 \\\\ - 28 u - 1 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe critical points lie on the plane $- 28 u - 1=0.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186528128 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5eb95208-de1d-5107-937c-4b95392cabfb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $4 u + 1=0.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528095} {:answer/id #uuid "8b151ea6-6bf3-50da-b2cf-48829c626b71" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $20 u - 2=0.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528108} {:answer/id #uuid "956a3402-0229-59fc-81ea-108ffa280642" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $28 u - 3=0.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528112} {:answer/id #uuid "f94ff84b-c560-53eb-b9d7-b92cca8a9bb4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $24 u - 2=0.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528139} {:answer/id #uuid "fa5273c3-d427-52c4-92ab-a1a09822e996" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $28 u - 2=0.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528141}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fa5273c3-d427-52c4-92ab-a1a09822e996" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $28 u - 2=0.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528141} :answer-field/id #uuid "179dd747-8255-5b2c-99ee-546770d66eeb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528080}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "dcb5cc43-b555-53b7-8a05-e6eed19a5fa4" :question/problem "Find the locations of all of the critical points of the transformation $T,$ where $T$ is defined as\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}u - 2 v + 3 w \\\\ u^{2} + v \\\\ - 4 u^{2} + u + w\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a transformation \n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} & \\frac{∂x}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v} & \\frac{∂y}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & \\frac{∂z}{∂v} & \\frac{∂z}{∂w}\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have \n\n$$\nx(u,v,w)=u - 2 v + 3 w,\\,y(u,v,w)=u^{2} + v,\\,z(u,v,w)=- 4 u^{2} + u + w.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =1 & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =-2 & \\frac{∂x}{∂w} & =3 \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =2 u & \\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =1 & \\frac{∂y}{∂w} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & =1 - 8 u & \\frac{∂z}{∂v} & =0 & \\frac{∂z}{∂w} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 2 u & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 - 8 u & 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(1)\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}+(2)\\begin{vmatrix}2 u & 0 \\\\ 1 - 8 u & 1\\end{vmatrix}+(3)\\begin{vmatrix}2 u & 1 \\\\ 1 - 8 u & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(1)(1\\cdot(1)-(0)\\cdot(0))+(2)(2 u\\cdot(1)-(0)\\cdot(1 - 8 u))+(3)(2 u\\cdot(0)-(1)\\cdot(1 - 8 u)) \\\\  & =2 \\left(14 u - 1\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function has critical points when $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}=0.$ So, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =0 \\\\ 2 \\left(14 u - 1\\right) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe critical points lie on the plane $28 u - 2=0.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186528131 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "45da639a-a9c4-5df9-b985-bd60ab49e03e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $22 u - 3=0.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528086} {:answer/id #uuid "4cccb54a-2323-54cc-8771-d66a1ea28d17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $10 u - 4=0.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528090} {:answer/id #uuid "a312df95-1798-5422-bdd8-51cc96fbf230" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $16 u - 3=0.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528114} {:answer/id #uuid "d2cddbd1-7645-57a2-987f-d4a400510d44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $1 - 6 u=0.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528127} {:answer/id #uuid "f11adf19-097e-5e21-9369-b018ddc048dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $10 u - 3=0.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528135}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f11adf19-097e-5e21-9369-b018ddc048dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $10 u - 3=0.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528135} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe2c2ef2-86c0-5fe7-bba6-8d0d09672c0b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528142}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "dee05f83-d6b9-5885-962f-b5d399b7ef4b" :question/problem "Find the locations of all of the critical points of the transformation $T,$ where $T$ is defined as\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}u + v - 4 w \\\\ 3 u^{2} + v \\\\ 2 u^{2} - u + w\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a transformation \n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} & \\frac{∂x}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v} & \\frac{∂y}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & \\frac{∂z}{∂v} & \\frac{∂z}{∂w}\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have \n\n$$\nx(u,v,w)=u + v - 4 w,\\,y(u,v,w)=3 u^{2} + v,\\,z(u,v,w)=2 u^{2} - u + w.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =1 & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =1 & \\frac{∂x}{∂w} & =-4 \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =6 u & \\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =1 & \\frac{∂y}{∂w} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & =4 u - 1 & \\frac{∂z}{∂v} & =0 & \\frac{∂z}{∂w} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 6 u & 1 & 0 \\\\ 4 u - 1 & 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(1)\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}+(-1)\\begin{vmatrix}6 u & 0 \\\\ 4 u - 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix}+(-4)\\begin{vmatrix}6 u & 1 \\\\ 4 u - 1 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(1)(1\\cdot(1)-(0)\\cdot(0))+(-1)(6 u\\cdot(1)-(0)\\cdot(4 u - 1))+(-4)(6 u\\cdot(0)-(1)\\cdot(4 u - 1)) \\\\  & =10 u - 3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function has critical points when $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}=0.$ So, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =0 \\\\ 10 u - 3 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe critical points lie on the plane $10 u - 3=0.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186528132 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6843c54c-f17b-5834-b153-e5b5a1efb011" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $u + 1=0.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528098} {:answer/id #uuid "74f168eb-ccb1-5380-b363-e871472ffa30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $v + 1=0.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528102} {:answer/id #uuid "b8a304f5-81ed-5e87-be99-54f35f1ec0bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $u - 1=0.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528122} {:answer/id #uuid "de769aee-8b75-51ef-a2c0-08755022682c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $w + 1=0.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528129} {:answer/id #uuid "f5b4dd00-64f4-5b00-8e49-b71031fa0857" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $u=0.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528136}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6843c54c-f17b-5834-b153-e5b5a1efb011" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $u + 1=0.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528098} :answer-field/id #uuid "813dd0bb-8482-5415-8c3e-9e6f5842ffd9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528104}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "dfb5d07b-82a7-5cc7-b48f-5f51fbec3e21" :question/problem "Find the locations of all of the critical points of the transformation $T,$ where $T$ is defined as\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}\\left(u + 1\\right)^{2} \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a transformation \n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} & \\frac{∂x}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v} & \\frac{∂y}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & \\frac{∂z}{∂v} & \\frac{∂z}{∂w}\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have \n\n$$\nx(u,v,w)=\\left(u + 1\\right)^{2},\\,y(u,v,w)=v,\\,z(u,v,w)=w.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =2 u + 2 & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =0 & \\frac{∂x}{∂w} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =0 & \\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =1 & \\frac{∂y}{∂w} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & =0 & \\frac{∂z}{∂v} & =0 & \\frac{∂z}{∂w} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}2 u + 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(2 u + 2)\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(2 u + 2)(1\\cdot(1)-(0)\\cdot(0)) \\\\  & =2 \\left(u + 1\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function has critical points when $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}=0.$ So, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =0 \\\\ 2 \\left(u + 1\\right) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe critical points lie on the plane $u + 1=0.$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Critical Points of a Transformation"}]}
